{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "text": "What does len() give for a string?",
      "options": [
        "How many words it has",
        "How many characters it has, spaces and signs included",
        "How many letters it has, without the spaces",
        "The position of its last character"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "name = \"Tommy Vercetti\"\nprint(len(name))",
      "options": ["14", "13", "2", "12"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "text": "Where does counting the positions of a string start?",
      "options": ["At 1", "At the last character", "At the first space", "At 0"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "text": "`name` holds \"Tommy\". What is `name[1]`?",
      "options": ["T", "m", "o", "Tommy"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "text": "What does `name.upper()` do to `name`?",
      "options": [
        "It turns name into capitals for good",
        "Nothing: it gives back a new string in capitals, and name stays as it was",
        "It prints name in capitals",
        "It stops with an error unless name is already in capitals"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "name = \"tommy\"\nname.upper()\nprint(name)",
      "options": ["tommy", "TOMMY", "Tommy", "Nothing"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "text": "Which line keeps `name` in capitals for good?",
      "options": ["name.upper()", "upper(name)", "name == name.upper()", "name = name.upper()"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "text": "What is a method, like `upper()` in `name.upper()`?",
      "options": [
        "A variable kept inside a string",
        "A keyword, like if",
        "A function that belongs to something, called after a dot",
        "A comment written after a line"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "text": "What does `+` do between two strings?",
      "options": [
        "It adds up their lengths",
        "It glues them into one string",
        "It puts a space between them and prints them",
        "It stops with an error: + is only for numbers"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q10",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "first = \"Star\"\nsecond = \"Ship\"\nprint(first + second)",
      "options": ["StarShip", "Star Ship", "Star+Ship", "first + second"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q11",
      "text": "Which line prints Tommy Vercetti, when `first_name` is \"Tommy\" and `last_name` is \"Vercetti\"?",
      "options": [
        "print(first_name + last_name)",
        "print(\"first_name last_name\")",
        "print(first_name + \"\" + last_name)",
        "print(first_name + \" \" + last_name)"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q12",
      "text": "What do we call gluing strings together with +?",
      "options": ["Indexing", "An iteration", "Concatenation", "A method"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q13",
      "text": "Which positions does `name[0:5]` take?",
      "options": ["0, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5", "0, 1, 2, 3 and 4", "1, 2, 3, 4 and 5", "Only 0 and 5"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q14",
      "text": "Why doesn't `name[0:5]` take the character at position 5?",
      "options": [
        "The end is left out, as with range()",
        "Python always skips the last letter of a word",
        "Position 5 is always a space",
        "It does take it: name[0:5] has 6 characters"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q15",
      "text": "`name` holds \"Tommy Vercetti\". What is `name[6:]`?",
      "options": ["Tommy", "V", "ercetti", "Vercetti"],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q16",
      "text": "`name` holds \"Tommy Vercetti\". What is `name[:5]`?",
      "options": ["Tomm", "Vercetti", "Tommy", "y"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q17",
      "text": "How many characters does `word[2:7]` take?",
      "options": ["7", "5", "6", "2"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q18",
      "text": "`name` holds \"Tommy Vercetti\". Which character is `name[9]`?",
      "options": ["c", "e", "t", "r"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q19",
      "text": "Does a space count in `len()`?",
      "options": [
        "No: len(\"a b\") is 2",
        "Only a space at the end",
        "Only inside an f-string",
        "Yes: len(\"a b\") is 3"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q20",
      "text": "Which line prints the first character of `word`?",
      "options": ["print(word[1])", "print(word(0))", "print(word[0])", "print(word[0:0])"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q21",
      "text": "In the Position Decoder mission the user types Andromeda. Which character is `word[3]`?",
      "options": ["d", "r", "o", "n"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q22",
      "text": "In the Position Decoder mission the user types Andromeda. What is `word[4:]`?",
      "options": ["omeda", "romeda", "meda", "Andr"],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
